[
  {
    "severity": "blocker",
    "title": "Pre-intent crash artifacts have no resource bound",
    "evidence": "§Actors and lease explicitly leaves unreferenced private stages after a crash before durable intent, but defines no cleanup, reuse, quota or admission limit for them. Repeated stage_fsynced crashes advance neither revision nor receipt count, so §Kernel's capacity limits do not apply. Existing actors.prepare_bootstrap creates randomly named .operator-*.stage and .intent-*.tmp files; StateStore stale cleanup covers only state temporary files. This triggers the cardinal sin prohibiting unbounded resource consumption.",
    "suggested_fix": "Define bounded staging slots under the existing exclusive lock, or a bounded orphan policy that refuses further preparation without discarding forensic evidence. Add repeated pre-intent crash tests proving file count and total bytes remain bounded."
  },
  {
    "severity": "non-blocker",
    "title": "Healthy intent recovery needs an explicit success criterion",
    "evidence": "§Actors and lease allows forward reconciliation 'or returns recovery_required retaining evidence', while §Test strategy requires existing recovery tests to pass. OwnerRecoveryTest.recover_matching accepts recovery_required and returns even after an intact injected crash. Consequently those acceptance tests can pass while ordinary crashes permanently require intervention. The bootstrap equivalent requires successful recovery.",
    "suggested_fix": "Specify successful exact-receipt recovery for every intact injected boundary. Reserve recovery_required for damaged, unverifiable or unsupported evidence, and require the owner recovery tests to distinguish these cases."
  },
  {
    "severity": "checked-correct",
    "title": "Historical receipt authority remains separate from mutation authority",
    "evidence": "§Protocol explicitly permits historical credentials, or the current credential for the same actor and role, to retrieve only an unchanged historical envelope. New operations require the current descriptor and epoch. This addresses the existing protocol.existing_open limitation, which authenticates only against the historical descriptor, and matches OwnerTest.test_historical_and_reopened_operator_retrieve_only_exact_receipts_after_all_rotations.",
    "suggested_fix": "None."
  },
  {
    "severity": "checked-correct",
    "title": "Capacity reserves have concrete terminal behavior",
    "evidence": "§Kernel distinguishes 4094 normal receipts from the 4096 hard ceiling, independently bounds normal serialized bytes, permits reserve consumption only while clearing an active owner, preserves receipts, and defines an archive/hash/restore/new-workflow procedure. These rules match the exact count, byte, no-owner, hard-capacity and archive scenarios in test_controller_capacity.py.",
    "suggested_fix": "None."
  },
  {
    "severity": "checked-correct",
    "title": "Restore deliberately prevents protocol rollback",
    "evidence": "§Kernel requires equality of lease_epoch, owner, actors and receipts under the exclusive lock and refuses pending credential intent. The pinned OVCAQ StateStore.restore otherwise accepts the prior backup after a current-state precondition, so the documented divergence is necessary and accurately identified. Existing kernel tests cover acquired-owner refusal, security-identical restoration, pending intent and boundary failures.",
    "suggested_fix": "None."
  }
]
